    {
      "id": "BYtC",
      "code_hash": "af7733a5a1a566d1a915b56196b34ae1",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>postcondition</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.bpm &gt;= 30)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.bpm &lt;= 230)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>~_.bpm.isnan()</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.ts &gt;= _.start)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.ts &lt; _.end)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>unique(user_id, ts)</code></td>\n<td>\u274c not shown to be a key</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>output column</th>\n<th>known values</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>user_id</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>kind</code></td>\n<td>a string or NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>ts</code></td>\n<td>any timestamp</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>bpm</code></td>\n<td>a double \u2265 30.0 and \u2264 230.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>start</code></td>\n<td>any timestamp</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>end</code></td>\n<td>any timestamp</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></span><marimo-callout-output data-html='&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cstrong&#92;u003eWarning:&#92;u003c/strong&#92;u003e The &#x27;future.infer_string&#x27; option is deprecated and will be removed in pandas 4.0. Inferring str dtype for string data has been the default since pandas 3.0, and it will no longer be possible to disable it.&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;' data-kind='&quot;warn&quot;'></marimo-callout-output></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "RGSE",
      "code_hash": "144903a2f6cda52f660a9d3ae1338e8c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"reading-the-verdicts\">Reading the verdicts</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>bpm &gt;= 30</code>, <code>bpm &lt;= 230</code></strong>: the filter keeps only those rows, and\n  Lean tracks the interval of every column through the plan.</li>\n<li><strong><code>~bpm.isnan()</code></strong>: subtle! There is no NaN check in the pipeline. But\n  DataFusion orders floats <em>totally</em>, with NaN above every number, so\n  <code>NaN &lt;= 230</code> is false and the filter already removes NaN. Lean models\n  DataFusion's floats exactly, so it knows this. Careful: unlike in\n  Python, <code>NaN &gt;= 30</code> is TRUE in DataFusion, so a lower bound alone would\n  let NaN through. Try it in section 3.</li>\n<li><strong><code>ts &gt;= start</code>, <code>ts &lt; end</code></strong>: the join condition holds for every\n  joined row, and <code>requires</code> says <code>start</code> and <code>end</code> are never NULL, so\n  the comparisons are TRUE rather than NULL.</li>\n<li><strong><code>unique(user_id, ts)</code>: refused, and rightly so.</strong> Each sample is unique\n  in <code>heart_rate</code>, but nothing stops a user from logging two <em>overlapping</em>\n  workouts; a sample inside both would appear twice. Lean finds no proof\n  because there is none. Section 4 makes the counterexample real.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The <strong>known values</strong> table is everything Lean derived about the output,\nwhether or not you asked: it is a free, proved data dictionary.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "95704322f8c69fc7b8cf219d4ac1b5fb",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"3-break-the-pipeline-watch-the-proof-go\">3. Break the pipeline, watch the proof go</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Change the filter and the postconditions below are re-proved on the fly.\nLower bounds under 30 lose <code>bpm &gt;= 30</code>; drop the upper bound and NaN\ngets through, so <code>~bpm.isnan()</code> fails as well.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
