    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "81317c8d9f6d0a6363cf4e87d6cfdb6d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"4-keep-it-up-to-date-incrementally\">4. Keep it up to date, incrementally</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">New samples arrive every few seconds; recomputing the join each time is\nwasteful. <code>sv.IncrementalView</code> asks Lean for <strong>delta plans</strong>: queries\nthat compute only the <em>change</em> to the result from the changes to the\ninputs. Lean proves that old result + change = new result, for every\ndatabase and every batch of changes.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The view below starts from the result of <code>workout_heart_rate</code>. Stream in\nsamples, and log an overlapping workout to see why <code>unique(user_id, ts)</code>\nwas refused.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
